Rationale: chameleon keeps its own orchestration (three-level resolution,
session/workspace bindings, picker) but delegates skin RENDERING to the
official engine semantics so third-party skins from dsh-market.com render
identically to dsh-web's skin center. Vendoring (vs forking at runtime)
keeps the tree-external plugin self-contained with zero runtime coupling to
the skin-center npm package.
